  No — HybridParallelPlugin supports 3D parallelism but it is NOT automatic. The two are fundamentally different:         
                                                                                                                          
  ┌────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐   
  │                        │            HybridParallelPlugin             │            Your auto 3D planner            │   
  ├────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ tp_size                │ You must provide it                         │ Searched automatically                     │   
  ├────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ pp_size                │ You must provide it                         │ Searched automatically                     │   
  ├────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Layer → stage          │ Equal split by default                      │ Optimized by alpa_dp to balance compute    │   
  │ assignment             │                                             │                                            │   
  ├────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ TP strategy per        │ Manual policy (via Shardformer + Policy     │ Solved by ILP in initialize_model()        │   
  │ operator               │ class)                                      │                                            │
  ├────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤   
  │ Cost-aware             │ No — takes whatever you give it             │ Yes — profiles α/β, minimizes end-to-end   │
  │                        │                                             │ time                                       │   
  └────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                                                                                          
  The docstring at line 932 says it explicitly: "The size of tp and pp should be passed in by user". It doesn't search,   
  profile, or optimize anything.
                                                                                                                          
  What HybridParallelPlugin actually does:
  1. Takes your manually specified tp_size and pp_size
  2. Applies a fixed Shardformer Policy (e.g., GPT2Policy) — a hand-written set of rules per model architecture that says 
  which layers to shard and how                                                                                          
  3. Splits layers equally across pipeline stages                                                                         
  4. Wires up the process groups                 
                                                                                                                          
  This means it requires a pre-written Policy class for every model — there's no generality. If you have a custom model   
  architecture, there's no policy for it and it won't work.                                                               
                                                                                                                          
  What your auto 3D planner adds:                                                                                         
  - Automatically finds tp_size, pp_size, dp_size from profiled hardware costs
  - Optimally assigns layers to stages (not equal split)                                                                  
  - Works on any model via FX tracing — no hand-written policy needed
  - The ILP solver picks the best per-operator sharding strategy                                                          
                                                                                                                          
  So HybridParallelPlugin is the execution engine — it knows how to run 3D parallel training. Your planner is the planning
   layer on top that automatically decides the configuration to hand to that engine. They are complementary, not          
  duplicates. 